{"id": "EUVD-2026-103717", "enisaUuid": "94d9fa34-9056-3f07-83d9-82f38b1ec9d9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf/core: Fix NULL pmu_ctx passed to pmu->sched_task()\n\nperf_pmu_sched_task() returns early when cpuctx->task_ctx is set, and\ncpc->task_epc is only non-NULL while a task context is scheduled in on\nthis CPU. __perf_pmu_sched_task() therefore always passes NULL:\n\n  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00\n  pc : armv8pmu_sched_task+0x14/0x50\n  Call trace:\n   armv8pmu_sched_task+0x14/0x50 (P)\n   perf_pmu_sched_task+0xac/0x108\n   __perf_event_task_sched_out+0x6c/0xe0\n\nPass &cpc->epc instead, the CPU-wide context for this PMU, which the\nfunction already dereferences a few lines up to find pmu.\n\narmv8pmu_sched_task() is the only in-tree implementation that\ndereferences the argument, and it only reads ->pmu, so the oops needs\nBRBE, added in v6.17.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98181f9721f75f1a544dc563b0d8fed1d5c398d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5409311b606d536cc485f3706c242c2afa93edb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/249a2bd87a0e57dc28f36e992807edc9cae309b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec15f6a50183fc01f470af74ad49900fb3731fca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36bb85cf36cab15fb611cb44b78a5df06e4e69a2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-23r4-4gr3-gjfw", "CVE-2026-98477"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "110fb501-1a84-3ac0-9b97-75d1b39b4a1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "11aac9a2-9e7a-3a74-8c0c-a47cf8570bec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <98181f9721f75f1a544dc563b0d8fed1d5c398d5"}, {"id": "2e2fb650-0b1a-3433-ac39-57165ea50621", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <249a2bd87a0e57dc28f36e992807edc9cae309b5"}, {"id": "596d8e35-71aa-3a34-9fd2-c7d9f0a92dfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "643f9b20-f326-3af3-995d-c96a87cccdec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <ec15f6a50183fc01f470af74ad49900fb3731fca"}, {"id": "6ea0c82c-c133-35da-9494-68351ffa694d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "b9c82627-7cc3-392f-a758-d1e10bf0e691", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}, {"id": "bcd6c0b8-c50e-3282-bdbd-05736853fdb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "c1e9aaf8-de09-3dc3-8061-db67ab4e788a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d7a621f0-50dd-3f56-a06d-79830ee0f2bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <36bb85cf36cab15fb611cb44b78a5df06e4e69a2"}, {"id": "e7be5a0e-9fa9-3d3a-a3a8-bcf2617b8dc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <b5409311b606d536cc485f3706c242c2afa93edb"}, {"id": "e9038d4d-1c92-31a6-b563-02558a293058", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "83e3e4d5-3c97-3a71-b417-dcca4ef0af9b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}